-## ⛔ MIGRATION BLOCKER — not implemented; do not deploy to any existing game
-
-`hit_chance_modifier` adds an **8-byte I32F32-backed field to `CharacterModifierSized`**, immediately before
-`#[unsized_start]` (the host test pins `size_of::<PackedValue<I32F32>>() == 8`; the
-full generated sized-header delta and alignment still need an old-byte fixture test).
-This shifts the unsized tail (`research_tags`, `cargo_categories`,
-`rare_mineral_discovery`) in EVERY account whose layout embeds a `CharacterModifier`:
-
-| Account | Impact |
-|---|---|
-| `Character` | sized header grows 4 B; tail offsets shift |
-| `CharacterSync` (staging) | same — staged `modifiers` mirror |
-| `ResearchTreeDefinitions` → `ResearchNode.modifier` | every node's bytes shift |
-
-Consequences:
-
-- **Existing mainnet accounts fail closed on decode** (borsh/bytemuck length + field
-  mismatch). That is the intended fail-closed posture, but it means the upgrade CANNOT be
-  installed over live state without a reserialization migration.
-- Required follow-up (deliberately NOT guessed at here): a governance-gated account
-  migration that rewrites each affected account with the new layout, defaulting
-  `hit_chance_modifier = 0` (I32F32 raw 0) for pre-existing accounts — i.e. existing
-  accounts qualify at exactly "0 tiers" and must NOT be credited any bonus. Any migration
-  MUST be written against the actual account census (sizes, page counts, padding) and
-  rehearsed on a mainnet-snapshot fixture before deployment. Writing it by guess was
-  explicitly out of scope for this branch.
-- Frozen-ABI / IDL regen and generated client crates (`clients/crates/...`) also need
-  regeneration once the layout lands — not done here (no chain writes, no SDK bump).
