+## Exact serialized layout change
+
+`hit_chance_modifier` is an eight-byte packed I32F32 field at offset 99 in
+`CharacterModifierSized`.
+
+| Type or representative payload | Before | After | Delta |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| `CharacterModifierSized` | 99 | 107 | +8 |
+| empty `CharacterModifier` | 111 | 119 | +8 |
+| default Character payload | 407 | 415 | +8 |
+| default CharacterSync payload | 189 | 197 | +8 |
+| default ResearchNode payload | 205 | 213 | +8 |
+| one-node ResearchTreeDefinitions payload | 227 | 235 | +8 |
+
+`CharacterSized` itself remains 282 bytes. The change is therefore **not** a four-byte
+Character sized-header extension. It is an eight-byte extension inside every embedded
+`CharacterModifier`, immediately before the unsized `research_tags`, `cargo_categories`,
+and `rare_mineral_discovery` tail.
+
+## ⛔ Old layouts are unsupported and do not universally fail closed
+
+Exact base bytes demonstrate two different failure modes under the new Rust layout:
+
+- old CharacterModifier, Character, and CharacterSync bytes reject with `RawSliceAdvance`;
+- an old one-node ResearchTreeDefinitions value is accepted but observed as zero nodes;
+- the old genesis Game is accepted but its 63-node research tree is observed as zero nodes;
+- the generated TypeScript decoder rejects that same old Game with
+  `Codec [u16] expected 2 bytes, got 1`.
+
+Therefore no universal fail-closed claim is valid. A successful Rust decode is not proof that
+old semantic content survived. Installing this program over an existing Game is explicitly
+unsupported by this branch.
+
+This branch does **not** implement live migration, reserialization, account versioning, or a
+general old-layout refusal mechanism. Existing deployed games remain excluded unless a separate,
+reviewed design is requested and delivered.
+
+## Fresh-genesis-only qualification gate
+
+The supported candidate path is a fresh local genesis assembled from exact selected Programs and
+Editor sources. Qualification must:
+
+1. generate new Game/Character bytes using the new layout; never restamp the old fixture;
+2. assert exact expected research-node count and IDs, including Targeting #469–472;
+3. decode the same fresh Game bytes through both the Rust and generated TypeScript decoders and
+   require identical expected node identities;
+4. execute real nonzero purchase → Character sync → attacker/counterfire behavior against the
+   matching built program and config;
+5. keep existing deployed Game addresses out of the deployment/target manifest.
+
+The final selected universe/genesis/fixture writer owns that proof. Source-only tests and this
+compatibility witness are necessary inputs, not E2E evidence.
+
+## Focused source evidence
+
+Focused host tests cover:
+
+- 0/1/2/3/4 tiers → 0/10k/20k/30k/40k PPM;
+- zero-tier parity with the legacy Q6 roll threshold;
+- +1pp and +4pp roll-threshold deltas;
+- maximum clamp at 1,000,000 PPM;
+- each side's own bonus for attacker and defender counterfire;
+- starbase exclusion;
+- additive CharacterModifier combine and research-tree sync;
+- C4 schema conversion/validation.
+
+Fixture, generated-TS Game decode, and combat-SBF CI remain red until the fresh-layout integration
+artifacts are produced. Do not describe this branch as release-qualified from host tests alone.
+
+## Producer decision
+
+Choose one path explicitly:
+
+1. **Fresh-only:** accept the deployed-game exclusion, merge the corrected documentation, and
+   require the fresh-genesis expected-node/dual-decoder guard during qualification; or
+2. **Separate refusal design:** request a bounded Programs change that explicitly rejects old
+   ResearchTree/Game layouts before gameplay. Do not infer that work from this documentation patch.
